    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Corbin Carroll** leads the charge with an elite score of 79.66, bolstered by an excellent matchup against Abbott, whose 5.01 xERA creates a prime environment for **Corbin Carroll** to utilize his elite speed and batting order advantage. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.92) is our second-most reliable start, benefiting significantly from a favorable platoon advantage against Waguespack, which adds 14% to his efficiency. Meanwhile, **Gabriel Moreno** (66.83) rounds out our top-tier plays; despite the platoon disadvantage against the lefty Abbott, the combination of his #3 spot in the order and the opposing starter\u2019s poor xERA keeps his floor high enough to anchor the middle of our lineup.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Isaac Paredes**, who posted a 43.29 efficiency score but ultimately missed the cut. While **Isaac Paredes** typically provides steady production, he was squeezed out by the high-ceiling matchups we have elsewhere, specifically the late-order power profiles of **Griffin Conine** and **Mickey Moniak**, who both benefit from more favorable park factors than the environment **Isaac Paredes** faces against Imanaga. We are also closely monitoring the lineup integrity for **Jose Caballero**; his raw projection is dampened by a steep -13% dynamic platoon penalty, but his 50% SB potential keeps him on the field despite an unfavorable #9 batting position.\n\nWe are operating with a cautious eye toward the weather and the high-leverage arms on the mound today. **Josh Naylor** faces a particularly stern test against Imanaga (3.69 xERA), forcing his score down to a marginal 48.74, while **Seiya Suzuki** must contend with a -11% penalty due to Miller\u2019s skill set. We continue to hold **Trevor Story** and **James Wood** on the IL, hoping for a return to health that would bolster our depth for the final push. Aside from the injuries, the main risk remains the efficiency of **Max Muncy**, who carries a marginal 59.01 score as he faces a tough assignment against Javier, though his positional utility keeps him locked into our starting infield for the time being.",
